window.RISK_WORD_BASELINE = {"detailed":["OT CYBER RISK ASSESSMENT","OT Cyber Risk","Assessment","Acme Petrochemicals Ltd","Acme Petrochemicals - Unit 300 Alkylation Control System","IEC 62443-3-2: zones, conduits and target security levels","ISSUE   1.0  ·  2026-07-01 to 2026-07-04        AUTHOR   S. Maesschalck        CLASSIFICATION   Confidential - Client Restricted","SolutionsPT Ltd   ·   Unit 1, Oakfield Road, Cheadle Royal Business Park, Cheadle, Cheshire SK8 3GX","Telephone +44 (0) 161 495 4600   ·   sales@solutionspt.com   ·   www.solutionspt.com","Document control","Client / organisation","Acme Petrochemicals Ltd","System under consideration","Acme Petrochemicals - Unit 300 Alkylation Control System","Consultant","S. Maesschalck","Assessment date","2026-07-01 to 2026-07-04","Document revision","1.0","QA review by","(not set)","Confidentiality","Confidential - Client Restricted","Method","IEC 62443-3-2, using the SolutionsPT house risk matrix and risk-to-SL mapping","Asset-owner sign-off","R. Calder (Asset Owner - Unit 300), 2026-07-04; S. Adeyemi (Process Safety Engineer), 2026-07-04","Executive summary","Why this assessment","A cyber incident on a plant can stop production, damage equipment and put people at risk. Regulators and insurers increasingly expect an asset owner to show where that risk sits and that the protection in place is proportionate to it. Acme Petrochemicals Ltd commissioned this assessment of Acme Petrochemicals - Unit 300 Alkylation Control System (2026-07-01 to 2026-07-04) to establish that.","The essential functions in scope are continuous closed-loop control of the alkylation reaction (temperature, acid ratio, pressure), operator view and command from the central control room, and the SIS safety instrumented functions (emergency depressurisation, acid feed isolation). The credible worst-case consequence is loss or manipulation of control or safety functions leading to an acid release or reactor overpressure: potential for multiple serious injuries on-site, off-site public exposure at the fence line, a COMAH-reportable event and multi-week unit outage. Risk in this report means the likelihood and severity of that outcome, not the loss of data or an IT service.","The assumed adversary is SL3 grade on the IEC 62443 scale, meaning a deliberate attacker who knows control systems, using purpose-built tools and a moderate budget. This choice is the asset owner&apos;s, because it sets how strong the countermeasures must be.","What this report is","The assessment follows IEC 62443-3-2. 6 systems were first ranked for relative risk. The system under consideration was then divided into 4 security zones and 3 conduits. A zone groups assets with the same security requirements, and a conduit is a communication path between zones. The initial risk of each zone and conduit was first compared with the tolerable risk of Medium. C1 and C3 were found not to need a detailed assessment, and their SL-T rests on the written justification. Threats to the others were rated for likelihood and impact, and every threat above the tolerable risk needs a recorded treatment decision. Each zone and conduit then has a target security level (SL-T), the protection it must be engineered and maintained to.","The findings are based on 4 interviews, 4 documents and 3 direct observations, all listed under Basis of assessment.","What we found","9 threats were registered; 7 exceed the tolerable risk of Medium before treatment. The most affected is Z1 Unit 300 BPCS (remote access), with 2. The highest unmitigated risk is High: An external attacker hijacks or rides the vendor remote access path to reach the DCS servers and issue control changes (Z1 Unit 300 BPCS).","Of the 7 threats above tolerable risk, 2 are reduced to within tolerable risk by countermeasures, 4 are being reduced with countermeasures and 1 is formally accepted by the asset owner. The register holds 5 existing and 2 planned countermeasures.","Accepted risk T8 (Z4): The legacy depropaniser configuration tool&apos;s shared account is misused, making an unauthorised controller change unattributable. The rationale is recorded in the threat register and should be revisited at the next assessment.","What happens next","The highest target security levels across the system are IAC SL3, UC SL3, SI SL3, DC SL3, RDF SL3, TRE SL3, RA SL3. The SL3 ceiling is set by Z1 Unit 300 BPCS, Z2 Safety Instrumented System, Z4 Engineering workstations and 1 more. An IEC 62443-3-3 assessment against these targets will measure what the system can withstand today, and the gaps it finds become the security improvement programme.","Repeat this assessment after a significant change to the system or its connectivity, after a security incident, and otherwise at regular intervals.","This assessment was signed off by R. Calder (Asset Owner - Unit 300) on 2026-07-04, for “I confirm the tolerable risk of Medium used in this assessment reflects Acme&apos;s corporate risk criteria for Unit 300, and I accept the assessment outcome: the recorded treatment decisions, the residual risk positions, the one recorded risk acceptance (legacy configuration tooling), and the per-FR SL-T vectors as the target for the security programme”; and by S. Adeyemi (Process Safety Engineer) on 2026-07-04, for “The SL-T of the Safety Instrumented System zone (Z2)”.","Consultant note: tailor this summary before issue. Add the business context and engagement drivers, confirm the wording of any risk acceptances with the asset owner, and set out the agreed next steps. Delete this note.","Risk at a glance","9","threats registered","7","above tolerable (Medium)","7/7","with a treatment decision","SL3","highest SL-T set","Threats per zone and conduit by unmitigated risk band. The tolerable risk is Medium.","Risk profile by zone and conduit","Z1 Unit 300 BPCS","Z2 Safety Instrumented System","Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian","Z4 Engineering workstations","C1 Historian replication","C2 Vendor remote access","C3 Corporate reporting","■ Very high      ■ High      ■ Medium      ■ Low      ","Target security levels: worst case per foundational requirement","SL3","IAC","SL3","UC","SL3","SI","SL3","DC","SL3","RDF","SL3","TRE","SL3","RA","Where to focus first","1","T1  An external attacker hijacks or rides the vendor remote access path to reach the DCS servers and issue control changes.","Z1 · High","2","T2  Malware introduced through an engineering connection executes on a DCS server and corrupts control logic or displays.","Z1 · High","3","T4  An unauthorised or malicious logic change to the SIS defeats or degrades a safety instrumented function.","Z2 · High","System under consideration and requirements","The basic process control system, safety instrumented system and supporting OT infrastructure for the Unit 300 alkylation unit at the Teesport refinery: redundant SCADA/DCS servers and operator HMIs in the central control room, unit PLCs and remote I/O in the field auxiliary rooms, the SIS performing the unit&apos;s safety instrumented functions, engineering workstations, and the plant DMZ carrying the historian and vendor access paths.","Scope: In scope: all Unit 300 control, safety and engineering systems from the field controllers up to (and including) the plant DMZ, plus the conduits that cross the boundary (historian replication, vendor remote access, corporate reporting). Out of scope: the corporate IT network beyond the DMZ firewall, other process units, and the terminal loading systems (separately assessed).","Essential functions: Continuous closed-loop control of the alkylation reaction (temperature, acid ratio, pressure), operator view and command from the central control room, and the SIS safety instrumented functions (emergency depressurisation, acid feed isolation).","Worst-case consequence: Loss or manipulation of control or safety functions leading to an acid release or reactor overpressure: potential for multiple serious injuries on-site, off-site public exposure at the fence line, a COMAH-reportable event and multi-week unit outage.","Security functions that must be kept","SIS must remain capable of safe shutdown independent of BPCS state","Operator view and manual command must survive loss of the DMZ and corporate links","All remote access must be individually attributed and time-bounded","Zone and conduit drawings","Zone and conduit characteristics","These are the zones and conduits as defined for this assessment. Where a zone holds assets that are normally kept apart and they are not separated, the reason follows its table.","Z1: Unit 300 BPCS","Function","Continuous process control and operator interface for Unit 300.","Logical boundary","DCS servers, operator HMIs and unit PLCs performing closed-loop control of the alkylation unit.","Physical boundary","Central control room (DCS servers and HMIs) and field auxiliary rooms 1 and 3 (unit PLCs).","Accountable organisation","Acme Petrochemicals, Unit 300 operations","Safety designation","Not safety related","Assets","DCS server pair (redundant) (Server); Operator HMIs x4 (HMI); Unit PLCs x6 (reactor, acid feed, depropaniser) (PLC)","Logical access points","Vendor VPN via jump host (C2); Historian replication to DMZ (C1)","Physical access points","Control room door, badge controlled and logged; Field auxiliary rooms 1 and 3, keyed and on the operator round","Data flows","Process values to the historian through the OPC UA broker (C1); Vendor diagnostic sessions through the jump host (C2)","Conduits","C1 Historian replication to Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian; C2 Vendor remote access to Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian","External dependencies","DCS vendor support contract (remote diagnostics); Time sync from DMZ NTP","Security policies","No engineering changes without MoC approval; Vendor sessions activated per ticket, time-bounded","Assumptions","The control network carries no traffic from outside the zone other than C1 and C2","Exposure","Remote access","Z2: Safety Instrumented System","Function","Safety instrumented functions for Unit 300 (SIL 2 per LOPA).","Logical boundary","The SIS logic solver and safety I/O performing emergency depressurisation and acid feed isolation.","Physical boundary","Field auxiliary room 2, SIS cabinets.","Accountable organisation","Acme Petrochemicals, process safety","Safety designation","Safety related","Assets","SIS logic solver (Safety PLC); Safety I/O and final elements","Logical access points","Engineering connection from Z4 (keyed, normally disconnected)","Physical access points","Field auxiliary room 2, keyed, keys held by the shift supervisor","Data flows","Hardwired trip and status signals to the BPCS (no network path)","External dependencies","SIS vendor for logic changes (site visit only, no remote path)","Security policies","SIS changes require process safety authorisation and a keyed bypass record; No shared network segments with BPCS","Assumptions","The SIS program-mode keyswitch stays in run outside authorised changes","Z3: Plant DMZ &amp; historian","Function","Data brokerage and controlled external access; no control function.","Logical boundary","The brokered exchange layer between OT and corporate: process historian, patch/AV staging, NTP, and the vendor jump host.","Physical boundary","Server room, OT racks 4 and 5.","Accountable organisation","Acme Petrochemicals, OT network team","Safety designation","Not safety related","Assets","Process historian (primary) (Historian); Vendor jump host (Server); DMZ firewall pair (Network device)","Logical access points","Corporate reporting clients (C3); Historian replication from Z1 (C1); Vendor VPN termination (C2)","Physical access points","Server room door, badge controlled and shared with IT","Data flows","Process values in from the BPCS (C1); Read-only reports out to corporate clients (C3); Vendor VPN sessions in, onward through the jump host (C2)","Conduits","C1 Historian replication to Z1 Unit 300 BPCS; C2 Vendor remote access to Z1 Unit 300 BPCS; C3 Corporate reporting to external","External dependencies","Corporate AD federation for jump-host MFA; Vendor VPN concentrator availability","Security policies","All OT-corporate exchange transits the DMZ; no direct paths; DMZ hosts patched monthly (IT window)","Assumptions","The corporate network beyond the DMZ firewall is untrusted","Exposure","Remote access, internet adjacent, many conduits","Z4: Engineering workstations","Function","Configuration, programming and maintenance of all Unit 300 control and safety systems.","Logical boundary","Engineering workstations and configuration management for DCS, PLC and SIS tooling.","Physical boundary","Control building engineering office.","Accountable organisation","Acme Petrochemicals, control systems engineering","Safety designation","Not safety related","Assets","Engineering workstations x3 (Engineering workstation); Config management server (backups, versioning) (Server); Vendor laptops (turnarounds) (Engineering workstation), temporarily connected","Logical access points","Removable media (controlled USB process); Engineering VLAN to Z1 controllers","Physical access points","Engineering office door, badge controlled; USB media kiosk in the engineering office","Data flows","Configuration downloads to the BPCS controllers over the engineering VLAN; Keyed engineering connection to the SIS for authorised changes","External dependencies","Vendor licence dongles and offline update bundles","Security policies","USB media scanned at the kiosk before OT use; Engineering accounts are individual; admin by exception","Assumptions","Vendor laptops are only connected under a permit during turnarounds","Exposure","Removable media","Temporarily connected devices are not kept separate. Vendor laptops join the engineering VLAN during turnarounds after the media kiosk check. A separate maintenance zone is planned for the Q2-2027 turnaround.","C1: Historian replication","Ends","Z1 Unit 300 BPCS and Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian","Direction","One way, Z1 Unit 300 BPCS to Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian","Channels and protocols","OPC UA","Boundary devices","OPC UA broker; DMZ firewall pair","Notes","One-way logical replication from the BPCS to the DMZ historian via the OPC UA broker; no writes toward Z1.","C2: Vendor remote access","Ends","Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian and Z1 Unit 300 BPCS","Direction","One way, Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian to Z1 Unit 300 BPCS","Channels and protocols","VPN, RDP through the jump host","Boundary devices","Vendor VPN concentrator; Vendor jump host; DMZ firewall pair","Connection","External network (DCS vendor support engineers)","Notes","Vendor VPN terminates in the DMZ; sessions reach Z1 only via the recorded jump host, activated per ticket.","C3: Corporate reporting","Ends","Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian and external","Direction","One way, Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian to external","Channels and protocols","HTTPS","Boundary devices","DMZ firewall pair","Connection","External network (Acme corporate reporting clients)","Notes","Read-only reporting from the historian to corporate clients; corporate side is out of scope (untrusted by assumption).","Operating environment assumptions","Physical access to the control room and field auxiliary rooms is badge-controlled and logged","The corporate network is assumed compromised for the purposes of this assessment (untrusted)","Unit 300 operates continuously; a control-system outage forces a manual unit shutdown within 30 minutes","Vendor support for the DCS is contractually required and uses the remote access path assessed here","Known or presumed threats","Assumed adversary: SL3-grade","Capable criminal/ransomware adversary reaching OT via corporate IT or vendor access","State-capable adversary interest in refining sector (assumed class 3 for this SUC)","Insider misuse of engineering access (contractor churn on turnarounds)","Commodity malware ingress via removable media and engineering laptops","Organisational security policies","Acme Group OT cyber security standard GS-104 (zones, remote access, removable media)","Teesport permit-to-work and management of change procedures","Acme Group incident response plan, OT annex","Tolerable risk","Tolerable risk: Medium","Confirmed with the asset owner. The risk matrix, its scales and the tolerable line are in the appendix, Risk criteria.","Regulatory requirements","COMAH upper tier (major accident hazard) - HSE","NIS Regulations as designated OES for fuel supply","Basis of assessment","People interviewed","Name","Role","Date","Notes","R. Calder","Asset Owner - Unit 300","2026-07-01","Tolerable risk, worst case, business context","J. Whitmore","Lead Control Systems Engineer","2026-07-01","Architecture, engineering practice, vendor access","S. Adeyemi","Process Safety Engineer","2026-07-02","SIS functions, safety requirement spec, LOPA linkage","M. Kowalski","OT/IT Network Engineer","2026-07-02","DMZ design, firewall rules, historian replication","Documents reviewed","Title","Reference","Source","Relevance","Unit 300 P&amp;IDs and cause &amp; effect matrix","U300-CE-014 r7","Process safety files","SIS functions and safety-relevant control loops","OT network diagram - Teesport","NET-OT-002 r4","OT engineering","Zone and conduit partitioning baseline","Vendor remote access procedure","OPS-PROC-118","Operations","Remote access threat scenarios and existing countermeasures","COMAH safety report extract - Unit 300","COMAH-U300-2025","HSE submission","Worst-case consequence calibration","Systems and evidence observed","What was observed","Location","Date","Notes","Control room and field auxiliary room walkdown","Unit 300","2026-07-01","Badge control verified; unlocked engineering cabinet noted and raised","DMZ firewall rule review at the console","Server room","2026-07-02","Rules match diagram; two stale vendor rules removed during review","Vendor remote access session demonstration","Control building","2026-07-02","Session activation, attribution and recording observed end-to-end","High-level risk ranking","Systems are ranked by consequence and likelihood on the SolutionsPT house risk matrix. An arrow marks the zones a system is assigned to.","System","Function / location","Consequence","Likelihood","Risk","Note","Unit 300 BPCS (DCS servers, HMIs, unit PLCs)  → Z1","Closed-loop control and operator interface - control room / field aux rooms","Serious","Medium","High","Primary control layer; loss forces manual shutdown, manipulation is the acid-release path. Assigned to Z1, where a detailed assessment is required.","Safety Instrumented System (SIS)  → Z2","Emergency depressurisation and acid isolation - field aux room 2","Severe","Low","High","Last line of defence; any compromise is intolerable regardless of likelihood. Assigned to Z2, where a detailed assessment is required.","Plant DMZ &amp; process historian  → Z3","Data brokerage between OT and corporate - server room","Serious","Medium","High","Every external path transits here; a foothold pivots into the BPCS. Assigned to Z3, where a detailed assessment is required.","Engineering workstations &amp; config management  → Z4","DCS/PLC/SIS configuration - control building office","Serious","Medium","High","Holds the keys to every controller; removable media and legacy tooling in routine use. Assigned to Z4, where a detailed assessment is required.","Laboratory information system link","Sample results feed to the historian - lab","Serious","Low","Medium","One-way feed, no control path; ranked medium, monitored at high level only.","CCTV &amp; physical security systems","Site perimeter and unit cameras - site-wide","Negligible","High","Low","Commodity IP kit, frequently probed, but no process consequence; ranked low, so not taken to a detailed assessment.","Risk comparison","The initial risk of each zone and conduit was compared with the tolerable risk of Medium to decide where a detailed risk assessment is needed. Comparing each zone and conduit is the method used in this assessment. A zone&apos;s initial risk is the worst of the ranked systems assigned to it, or the rating entered for it. A conduit takes the higher initial risk of the zones it joins, unless a rating is entered for it.","Zone or conduit","Initial risk","Against tolerable risk","Detailed assessment","Reason","Z1 Unit 300 BPCS","High","Above","Required","Z2 Safety Instrumented System","High","Above","Required","Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian","High","Above","Required","Z4 Engineering workstations","High","Above","Required","C1 Historian replication","High","Above","Not required","One-way replication through the OPC UA broker. Its exposure is the Z3 pivot path, assessed there as T5, so the SL-T is set from the zones it joins.","C2 Vendor remote access","High","Above","Required","C3 Corporate reporting","High","Above","Not required","Read-only reporting to the out-of-scope corporate network. The exposure is assessed at the Z3 boundary (T5, T6).","Zones, conduits and the detailed risk assessment","Each threat is rated for likelihood and impact on the SolutionsPT house risk matrix and compared with the tolerable risk of Medium. The drawing and each zone&apos;s and conduit&apos;s characteristics are under System under consideration and requirements.","Z1: Unit 300 BPCS","Vulnerabilities: DCS servers on an extended-support OS awaiting the vendor&apos;s qualified upgrade path · OPC DA (legacy) still enabled alongside OPC UA for two displaced clients","Threat","L × I","Risk","Residual","Treatment","T1  An external attacker hijacks or rides the vendor remote access path to reach the DCS servers and issue control changes.  (External attacker via vendor access)  [IAC, RDF]","High × Serious","High","Medium","Reduced to within tolerable risk","T2  Malware introduced through an engineering connection executes on a DCS server and corrupts control logic or displays.  (Commodity malware via engineering path)  [SI]","Medium × Serious","High","Not rated","Reduce with countermeasures","T3  A flooding or resource-exhaustion event on the control network degrades operator view of the unit.  (Network fault or deliberate DoS)  [RA]","Low × Serious","Medium","Not rated","Within tolerable risk","Countermeasures: M1 Per-session vendor access activation with MFA and session recording on the jump host [existing] (IAC, UC, RDF) · M2 Application allow-listing on DCS servers and HMIs (vendor-qualified build) [existing] (SI) · M3 Retire OPC DA: migrate the two remaining clients to OPC UA through the DMZ broker [planned] (RDF, SI)","Z2: Safety Instrumented System","Vulnerabilities: SIS engineering software runs on a Z4 workstation that also carries DCS tooling (shared engineering asset)","Threat","L × I","Risk","Residual","Treatment","T4  An unauthorised or malicious logic change to the SIS defeats or degrades a safety instrumented function.  (Insider or attacker with engineering access)  [IAC, SI]","Low × Severe","High","Not rated","Reduce with countermeasures","Countermeasures: M4 Hardwired keyswitch required for SIS program mode; position alarmed to the control room [existing] (IAC, UC, SI)","Z3: Plant DMZ &amp; historian","Vulnerabilities: Historian web interface reachable from the whole corporate network, not just the reporting subnet","Threat","L × I","Risk","Residual","Treatment","T5  A compromised corporate client exploits the historian and uses it as a pivot toward the BPCS replication path.  (Attacker on corporate network)  [RDF, SI]","Medium × Serious","High","Not rated","Reduce with countermeasures","T6  Process data is exfiltrated from the historian (recipe and throughput confidentiality).  (Attacker on corporate network)  [DC]","Low × Serious","Medium","Not rated","Within tolerable risk","Countermeasures: M5 Restrict historian web access to the reporting subnet and put it behind the corporate SSO proxy [planned] (IAC, RDF)","Z4: Engineering workstations","Vulnerabilities: Legacy configuration tool for the depropaniser PLCs requires a shared local account and runs unsupported","Threat","L × I","Risk","Residual","Treatment","T7  Malware carried on removable media or a vendor laptop executes on an engineering workstation and spreads to controllers.  (Commodity malware via media/laptops)  [SI, RDF]","Medium × Serious","High","Not rated","Reduce with countermeasures","T8  The legacy depropaniser configuration tool&apos;s shared account is misused, making an unauthorised controller change unattributable.  (Insider misuse / contractor churn)  [UC]","Medium × Serious","High","Not rated","Risk accepted","T8 risk acceptance: Accepted by R. Calder (Asset Owner) 2026-07-04: the tool is retired at the Q2-2027 turnaround with the PLC upgrade; until then the workstation is isolated on the engineering VLAN, the account password is held by the shift supervisor and issued per use with a written record. Risk accepted at High for this bounded period.","Countermeasures: M6 Media kiosk scanning plus workstation allow-listing for engineering tools [existing] (SI, RDF)","C1: Historian replication  (Z1 → Z3)","No threats registered.","C2: Vendor remote access  (Z3 → Z1)","Threat","L × I","Risk","Residual","Treatment","T9  A vendor credential or session is hijacked and replayed to reach the DCS outside an authorised window.  (External attacker via vendor access chain)  [IAC, RDF]","Medium × Serious","High","Medium","Reduced to within tolerable risk","Countermeasures: M7 MFA on VPN and jump host, per-ticket session activation, session recording, auto-disconnect at window end [existing] (IAC, UC, RDF)","C3: Corporate reporting  (Z3 → external)","No threats registered.","Target security levels (SL-T, per foundational requirement)","Each zone and conduit has one target per foundational requirement, set by the consultant from the risk assessment.","Zone / conduit","IAC","UC","SI","DC","RDF","TRE","RA","Z1 Unit 300 BPCS","SL3","SL2","SL3","SL1","SL3","SL2","SL2","Z2 Safety Instrumented System","SL3","SL3","SL3","SL3","SL3","SL3","SL3","Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian","SL2","SL2","SL2","SL2","SL2","SL2","SL1","Z4 Engineering workstations","SL2","SL2","SL3","SL1","SL2","SL1","SL1","C1 Historian replication","SL2","Not set","SL2","SL1","SL2","Not set","Not set","C2 Vendor remote access","SL3","SL2","Not set","Not set","SL3","SL2","Not set","C3 Corporate reporting","SL2","Not set","Not set","SL2","SL2","Not set","Not set","Worst case","SL3","SL3","SL3","SL3","SL3","SL3","SL3","Justification for Z1 Unit 300 BPCS","The worst unmitigated risks in this zone are High (vendor-path compromise T1, engineering-path malware T2) against a Medium tolerable risk, and the standing remote access materially raises likelihood on IAC/UC/RDF, so IAC, SI and RDF are set to SL3 in line with the suggestion trace. UC is held at SL2 because use control inside the control room is procedurally constrained and no High risk hits it directly. DC reflects the low confidentiality consequence of process data (SL1). TRE and RA at SL2 support forensics and the 30-minute manual-shutdown resilience requirement. Targets are the treatment plan; capability is built through the 62443-3-3 programme this assessment exports to.","Justification for Z2 Safety Instrumented System","The SIS floor applies: a zone containing safety instrumented functions takes SL3 across every foundational requirement regardless of the per-threat arithmetic, because the SIS is the last line of defence and severe-consequence/low-likelihood events dominate. The one registered threat (T4, High risk) is reduced by the existing hardwired keyswitch (M4), and this SL-T vector sets the level the zone is held to. This vector is deliberately not averaged down: any relaxation requires the asset owner to re-open the sign-off.","Justification for Z3 Plant DMZ &amp; historian","The zone&apos;s worst unmitigated risk is High (T5 pivot toward the BPCS) with internet adjacency and many-conduit exposure traced on RDF/SI, but the DMZ exists precisely to absorb that exposure, and the planned historian access restriction (M5) addresses the driving vulnerability. SL2 across the access, integrity and data-flow FRs reflects the brokerage role; RA stays at SL1 because loss of the DMZ does not remove operator view or control (a security function that must be kept: the unit runs through a DMZ outage). The exfiltration threat T6 sits within tolerable risk and needs no treatment decision.","Justification for Z4 Engineering workstations","SI is set to SL3: the engineering zone is the integrity chokepoint for every controller and the removable-media exposure is traced against a High malware risk (T7), mitigated in day-to-day terms by the existing kiosk-plus-allow-listing countermeasures (M6). The shared-account threat (T8) exceeds tolerable risk and carries a recorded, time-bounded risk acceptance by the asset owner rather than an SL uplift: the compensating procedure and the Q2-2027 retirement are the treatment. Remaining FRs sit at SL1-2 consistent with no external paths into this zone.","Justification for C1 Historian replication","Carries the Z3 pivot risk (T5) as its data-flow path: SL2 on IAC/SI/RDF matches the zone targets either side; the broker enforces direction so no higher target is warranted.","Justification for C2 Vendor remote access","This conduit is the highest-exposure path into the BPCS: the hijack threat (T9) starts High and the existing per-session countermeasures (M7) bring the residual within tolerable, but the SL-T is held at SL3 on IAC/RDF to match the Z1 targets it lands in, so the conduit is not the weak link. TRE at SL2 preserves the session-recording evidence chain.","Justification for C3 Corporate reporting","Boundary conduit to the untrusted corporate network: SL2 on IAC/DC/RDF reflects the read-only brokerage and the confidentiality of throughput data; no control traffic exists on this path.","Sign-off","Signed off as below. An approval covers the tolerable risk, the target security levels and the accepted risks in this report, within the scope given for it.","Approver","Role","Organisation","Scope","Date","Revision","R. Calder","Asset Owner - Unit 300","Acme Petrochemicals Ltd","I confirm the tolerable risk of Medium used in this assessment reflects Acme&apos;s corporate risk criteria for Unit 300, and I accept the assessment outcome: the recorded treatment decisions, the residual risk positions, the one recorded risk acceptance (legacy configuration tooling), and the per-FR SL-T vectors as the target for the security programme.","2026-07-04","1.0","S. Adeyemi","Process Safety Engineer","Acme Petrochemicals Ltd","The SL-T of the Safety Instrumented System zone (Z2).","2026-07-04","1.0","Method and limitations","The assessment follows IEC 62443-3-2:2020. The risk matrix, likelihood scale and risk-to-SL mapping are SolutionsPT house defaults. The standard prescribes no matrix, so a client corporate matrix takes precedence where one exists. Each SL-T is the consultant&apos;s judgement, informed by the house mapping.","Likelihood and impact ratings reflect the evidence available at the time of the engagement. The assessment sets targets and does not test security capability, which is measured against the SL-T in an IEC 62443-3-3 assessment.","Appendix: risk criteria","The SolutionsPT house risk criteria used in this assessment.","Risk matrix","Impact, by likelihood","Low","Medium","High","Severe","High (above)","High (above)","Very high (above)","Serious","Medium","High (above)","High (above)","Minor","Low","Medium","Medium","Negligible","Low","Low","Low","Tolerable risk is Medium. Cells marked above, with a heavy border, are above it: a threat rated there needs a recorded treatment decision.","Impact scale","Level","Meaning","Severe","Loss of life, a major release, loss of an essential function, or catastrophic cost or regulatory exposure.","Serious","Injury, reportable release, multi-shift outage, material cost, or regulatory action.","Minor","First aid only, a short outage, a small cost or a minor reportable event, recoverable within a shift.","Negligible","No meaningful safety, environmental, operational, financial or regulatory effect.","Likelihood scale","Level","Meaning","High","Known-exploited path, an exposed access point, or an actively targeted asset; expected without intervention.","Medium","Plausible given the exposure and a capable adversary; occurrence would not be surprising over the system&apos;s life.","Low","No known history; would require an unlikely combination of access, capability and intent.","Security levels","Security level","Protects against","SL1","Mistakes and chance misuse, with no intent to cause harm.","SL2","A deliberate attacker with general IT skills, simple tools and little time or money.","SL3","A deliberate attacker who knows control systems, using purpose-built tools and a moderate budget.","SL4","A deliberate attacker who knows control systems in depth and has the backing of a large organisation, such as a state.","The house mapping suggests an SL-T from the unmitigated risk: Low SL1, Medium SL2, High SL3, Very high SL3. SL4 is considered only where a nation-state-grade adversary is in scope.","Foundational requirements","Short form","Foundational requirement","IAC","FR1 Identification and authentication control","UC","FR2 Use control","SI","FR3 System integrity","DC","FR4 Data confidentiality","RDF","FR5 Restricted data flow","TRE","FR6 Timely response to events","RA","FR7 Resource availability"],"highLevel":["OT CYBER RISK ASSESSMENT","High-Level OT Cyber","Risk Assessment","Acme Petrochemicals Ltd","Acme Petrochemicals - Unit 300 Alkylation Control System","IEC 62443-3-2: high-level risk assessment and system ranking","ISSUE   1.0  ·  2026-07-01 to 2026-07-04        AUTHOR   S. Maesschalck        CLASSIFICATION   Confidential - Client Restricted","SolutionsPT Ltd   ·   Unit 1, Oakfield Road, Cheadle Royal Business Park, Cheadle, Cheshire SK8 3GX","Telephone +44 (0) 161 495 4600   ·   sales@solutionspt.com   ·   www.solutionspt.com","Document control","Client / organisation","Acme Petrochemicals Ltd","System under consideration","Acme Petrochemicals - Unit 300 Alkylation Control System","Consultant","S. Maesschalck","Assessment date","2026-07-01 to 2026-07-04","Document revision","1.0","QA review by","(not set)","Confidentiality","Confidential - Client Restricted","Method","IEC 62443-3-2 high-level risk assessment, using the SolutionsPT house risk matrix","Asset-owner sign-off","R. Calder (Asset Owner - Unit 300), 2026-07-04; S. Adeyemi (Process Safety Engineer), 2026-07-04","Executive summary","Why this assessment","A cyber incident on a plant can stop production, damage equipment and put people at risk. Before investing in detailed security engineering, Acme Petrochemicals Ltd needs to know which systems across Acme Petrochemicals - Unit 300 Alkylation Control System carry the most risk, and which justify a detailed assessment.","The essential functions in scope are continuous closed-loop control of the alkylation reaction (temperature, acid ratio, pressure), operator view and command from the central control room, and the SIS safety instrumented functions (emergency depressurisation, acid feed isolation). The credible worst-case consequence is loss or manipulation of control or safety functions leading to an acid release or reactor overpressure: potential for multiple serious injuries on-site, off-site public exposure at the fence line, a COMAH-reportable event and multi-week unit outage. Risk in this report means the likelihood and severity of that outcome, not the loss of data or an IT service.","The assumed adversary is SL3 grade on the IEC 62443 scale, meaning a deliberate attacker who knows control systems, using purpose-built tools and a moderate budget. This choice is the asset owner&apos;s, because it sets how strong the countermeasures must be.","What this report is","This is the first tier of an IEC 62443-3-2 risk assessment, the high-level cyber security risk assessment, carried out 2026-07-01 to 2026-07-04. Each system in scope was ranked by the consequence and likelihood of its compromise, and the resulting risk band compared with the tolerable risk of Medium. The ranking is relative. It puts the systems in priority order but does not measure absolute risk or set security targets.","The findings are based on 4 interviews, 4 documents and 3 direct observations, all listed under Basis of assessment.","What we found","6 systems were ranked: 4 High, 1 Medium, 1 Low. The systems above the tolerable risk of Medium (Unit 300 BPCS (DCS servers, HMIs, unit PLCs), Safety Instrumented System (SIS), Plant DMZ &amp; process historian, Engineering workstations &amp; config management) are the candidates for a detailed assessment; 4 ranked systems are in zones taken to a detailed assessment.","What happens next","Next, the systems are grouped into security zones and conduits, and the initial risk of each zone and conduit is compared with the tolerable risk to decide where a detailed assessment is needed. There, threats are registered and treated, and target security levels are set to scope the engineering work. Systems below the threshold should be re-ranked if their connectivity, criticality or threat exposure changes.","This assessment was signed off by R. Calder (Asset Owner - Unit 300) on 2026-07-04, for “I confirm the tolerable risk of Medium used in this assessment reflects Acme&apos;s corporate risk criteria for Unit 300, and I accept the assessment outcome: the recorded treatment decisions, the residual risk positions, the one recorded risk acceptance (legacy configuration tooling), and the per-FR SL-T vectors as the target for the security programme”; and by S. Adeyemi (Process Safety Engineer) on 2026-07-04, for “The SL-T of the Safety Instrumented System zone (Z2)”.","Consultant note: tailor this summary before issue. Add the business context and engagement drivers, confirm the wording of any risk acceptances with the asset owner, and set out the agreed next steps. Delete this note.","Risk at a glance","6","systems ranked","4","above tolerable risk","Medium","tolerable risk","4","for detailed assessment","Systems in scope ranked by consequence and likelihood on the SolutionsPT house risk matrix.","Systems by risk band","All ranked systems","■ Very high      ■ High      ■ Medium      ■ Low      ","Where to look first","1","Unit 300 BPCS (DCS servers, HMIs, unit PLCs)","High","2","Safety Instrumented System (SIS)","High","3","Plant DMZ &amp; process historian","High","System under consideration and requirements","The basic process control system, safety instrumented system and supporting OT infrastructure for the Unit 300 alkylation unit at the Teesport refinery: redundant SCADA/DCS servers and operator HMIs in the central control room, unit PLCs and remote I/O in the field auxiliary rooms, the SIS performing the unit&apos;s safety instrumented functions, engineering workstations, and the plant DMZ carrying the historian and vendor access paths.","Scope: In scope: all Unit 300 control, safety and engineering systems from the field controllers up to (and including) the plant DMZ, plus the conduits that cross the boundary (historian replication, vendor remote access, corporate reporting). Out of scope: the corporate IT network beyond the DMZ firewall, other process units, and the terminal loading systems (separately assessed).","Essential functions: Continuous closed-loop control of the alkylation reaction (temperature, acid ratio, pressure), operator view and command from the central control room, and the SIS safety instrumented functions (emergency depressurisation, acid feed isolation).","Worst-case consequence: Loss or manipulation of control or safety functions leading to an acid release or reactor overpressure: potential for multiple serious injuries on-site, off-site public exposure at the fence line, a COMAH-reportable event and multi-week unit outage.","Security functions that must be kept","SIS must remain capable of safe shutdown independent of BPCS state","Operator view and manual command must survive loss of the DMZ and corporate links","All remote access must be individually attributed and time-bounded","Operating environment assumptions","Physical access to the control room and field auxiliary rooms is badge-controlled and logged","The corporate network is assumed compromised for the purposes of this assessment (untrusted)","Unit 300 operates continuously; a control-system outage forces a manual unit shutdown within 30 minutes","Vendor support for the DCS is contractually required and uses the remote access path assessed here","Known or presumed threats","Assumed adversary: SL3-grade","Capable criminal/ransomware adversary reaching OT via corporate IT or vendor access","State-capable adversary interest in refining sector (assumed class 3 for this SUC)","Insider misuse of engineering access (contractor churn on turnarounds)","Commodity malware ingress via removable media and engineering laptops","Organisational security policies","Acme Group OT cyber security standard GS-104 (zones, remote access, removable media)","Teesport permit-to-work and management of change procedures","Acme Group incident response plan, OT annex","Tolerable risk","Tolerable risk: Medium","Confirmed with the asset owner. The risk matrix, its scales and the tolerable line are in the appendix, Risk criteria.","Regulatory requirements","COMAH upper tier (major accident hazard) - HSE","NIS Regulations as designated OES for fuel supply","Basis of assessment","People interviewed","Name","Role","Date","Notes","R. Calder","Asset Owner - Unit 300","2026-07-01","Tolerable risk, worst case, business context","J. Whitmore","Lead Control Systems Engineer","2026-07-01","Architecture, engineering practice, vendor access","S. Adeyemi","Process Safety Engineer","2026-07-02","SIS functions, safety requirement spec, LOPA linkage","M. Kowalski","OT/IT Network Engineer","2026-07-02","DMZ design, firewall rules, historian replication","Documents reviewed","Title","Reference","Source","Relevance","Unit 300 P&amp;IDs and cause &amp; effect matrix","U300-CE-014 r7","Process safety files","SIS functions and safety-relevant control loops","OT network diagram - Teesport","NET-OT-002 r4","OT engineering","Zone and conduit partitioning baseline","Vendor remote access procedure","OPS-PROC-118","Operations","Remote access threat scenarios and existing countermeasures","COMAH safety report extract - Unit 300","COMAH-U300-2025","HSE submission","Worst-case consequence calibration","Systems and evidence observed","What was observed","Location","Date","Notes","Control room and field auxiliary room walkdown","Unit 300","2026-07-01","Badge control verified; unlocked engineering cabinet noted and raised","DMZ firewall rule review at the console","Server room","2026-07-02","Rules match diagram; two stale vendor rules removed during review","Vendor remote access session demonstration","Control building","2026-07-02","Session activation, attribution and recording observed end-to-end","High-level risk ranking","Systems are ranked by consequence and likelihood on the SolutionsPT house risk matrix. An arrow marks the zones a system is assigned to.","System","Function / location","Consequence","Likelihood","Risk","Note","Unit 300 BPCS (DCS servers, HMIs, unit PLCs)  → Z1","Closed-loop control and operator interface - control room / field aux rooms","Serious","Medium","High","Primary control layer; loss forces manual shutdown, manipulation is the acid-release path. Assigned to Z1, where a detailed assessment is required.","Safety Instrumented System (SIS)  → Z2","Emergency depressurisation and acid isolation - field aux room 2","Severe","Low","High","Last line of defence; any compromise is intolerable regardless of likelihood. Assigned to Z2, where a detailed assessment is required.","Plant DMZ &amp; process historian  → Z3","Data brokerage between OT and corporate - server room","Serious","Medium","High","Every external path transits here; a foothold pivots into the BPCS. Assigned to Z3, where a detailed assessment is required.","Engineering workstations &amp; config management  → Z4","DCS/PLC/SIS configuration - control building office","Serious","Medium","High","Holds the keys to every controller; removable media and legacy tooling in routine use. Assigned to Z4, where a detailed assessment is required.","Laboratory information system link","Sample results feed to the historian - lab","Serious","Low","Medium","One-way feed, no control path; ranked medium, monitored at high level only.","CCTV &amp; physical security systems","Site perimeter and unit cameras - site-wide","Negligible","High","Low","Commodity IP kit, frequently probed, but no process consequence; ranked low, so not taken to a detailed assessment.","Sign-off","Signed off as below. An approval covers the tolerable risk and the ranking in this report, within the scope given for it.","Approver","Role","Organisation","Scope","Date","Revision","R. Calder","Asset Owner - Unit 300","Acme Petrochemicals Ltd","I confirm the tolerable risk of Medium used in this assessment reflects Acme&apos;s corporate risk criteria for Unit 300, and I accept the assessment outcome: the recorded treatment decisions, the residual risk positions, the one recorded risk acceptance (legacy configuration tooling), and the per-FR SL-T vectors as the target for the security programme.","2026-07-04","1.0","S. Adeyemi","Process Safety Engineer","Acme Petrochemicals Ltd","The SL-T of the Safety Instrumented System zone (Z2).","2026-07-04","1.0","Method and limitations","The assessment follows IEC 62443-3-2:2020. The risk matrix, likelihood scale and risk-to-SL mapping are SolutionsPT house defaults. The standard prescribes no matrix, so a client corporate matrix takes precedence where one exists.","Consequence and likelihood ratings reflect the evidence available at the time of the engagement. The assessment does not test security capability.","Appendix: risk criteria","The SolutionsPT house risk criteria used in this assessment.","Risk matrix","Impact, by likelihood","Low","Medium","High","Severe","High (above)","High (above)","Very high (above)","Serious","Medium","High (above)","High (above)","Minor","Low","Medium","Medium","Negligible","Low","Low","Low","Tolerable risk is Medium. Cells marked above, with a heavy border, are above it: a system rated there is a candidate for a detailed assessment.","Impact scale","Level","Meaning","Severe","Loss of life, a major release, loss of an essential function, or catastrophic cost or regulatory exposure.","Serious","Injury, reportable release, multi-shift outage, material cost, or regulatory action.","Minor","First aid only, a short outage, a small cost or a minor reportable event, recoverable within a shift.","Negligible","No meaningful safety, environmental, operational, financial or regulatory effect.","Likelihood scale","Level","Meaning","High","Known-exploited path, an exposed access point, or an actively targeted asset; expected without intervention.","Medium","Plausible given the exposure and a capable adversary; occurrence would not be surprising over the system&apos;s life.","Low","No known history; would require an unlikely combination of access, capability and intent.","Security levels","Security level","Protects against","SL1","Mistakes and chance misuse, with no intent to cause harm.","SL2","A deliberate attacker with general IT skills, simple tools and little time or money.","SL3","A deliberate attacker who knows control systems, using purpose-built tools and a moderate budget.","SL4","A deliberate attacker who knows control systems in depth and has the backing of a large organisation, such as a state."]};
